      "chart": "X=R^2/(2s), eta=Z/s^(1/2-h), s-Z^2*s^(2h)=T. Since s>0, ordinary real exponential power rules give 2*(1-eta^2)/X=4*(s-Z^2*s^(2h))/R^2=4T/R^2 throughout the smooth source chart. Equality on a neighborhood identifies all displayed slow derivatives; this is an analytic chart identity, not an evaluated inverse-root approximation.",
      "implicitZ": "The exact chart gives s_Z=0,s_ZZ=2 at Z=0,T=1. The reduced heat argument 4T/R^2 has no Z dependence. Thus F_Z=F_RZ=F_ZT=0 and F_ZZ=-2*B*(b*f+f_y)*H. The same exact Z-even equation supplies both mixed zeros.",
